      √ removed callback is called when lazy collection is not replaced
      √ blocked lazy collection is rejected before activation
      √ cached lazy collections are tracked correctly
    Duplicate Collection Prevention
      √ prevents duplicate non-lazy collections with same ID
      √ allows lazy collection to be replaced by non-lazy with same ID
      √ prevents lazy collection from duplicating existing non-lazy collection
      √ allows different collection IDs to coexist
      √ disposal of duplicate-preventing registration does not affect original
      √ simulates extension host restart scenario with when clause
    Server Label Collision Enablement
      √ disables lower-priority servers with same label
      √ does not disable servers with different labels
      √ label collision is case-insensitive
      √ respects collection order for priority
      √ enabling a colliding server disables others with same label
      √ no collision effect when behavior is "suffix"
      √ non-winner becomes enabled when winner is explicitly disabled
      √ updates when server definitions change
      √ three-way collision: only highest priority is enabled
      √ three-way collision: enabling lowest disables both others
      √ disabling winner cascades to next in priority
      √ both servers in same collection with same label: only first enabled
      √ EnabledWorkspace non-winner still suppressed if winner also enabled
      √ remove clears collision override and restores default behavior
      √ non-colliding servers in same collection as colliding ones are unaffected
      √ setEnabled with non-colliding server does not affect others
    Trust Flow
      √ trusted collection allows connection without prompting
      √ nonce-based trust allows connection when nonce matches
      √ nonce-based trust prompts when nonce changes
      √ nonce-based trust denies connection when user rejects
      √ autoTrustChanges bypasses prompt when nonce changes
      √ promptType "never" skips prompt and fails silently
      √ promptType "only-new" skips previously untrusted servers
      √ promptType "all-untrusted" prompts for previously untrusted servers
      √ concurrent resolveConnection calls with same interaction are grouped
      √ user cancelling trust dialog returns undefined for all pending connections
      √ partial trust selection in grouped interaction

